  "html": "<article class=\"markdown-body entry-content container-lg\" itemprop=\"text\"><p dir=\"auto\">D016 · Hints</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Use the hint for the point where you are stuck, then return to the task. Complete answers are grouped separately in <a href=\"/alverstris/PROF-Skill.md-/blob/51a78beccef858072b1da8d057ef3dff09878409/runs/y1-reader-20261008/iterations/016/published-r26-20261010/fresh-r26b/teaching/solutions.md\">solutions</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a id=\"user-content-h1\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hint P1. First mark the five endpoints of four equal pieces of <math-renderer class=\"js-inline-math\" style=\"display: inline-block\" data-run-id=\"4e8f0daad35909a96fa97a069126732f\" data-catalyst=\"\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo>\n</math></math-renderer>. For a left-endpoint sum, use the first four marks for the heights and leave the last mark unused. Each chosen height still needs multiplication by the common width. On one piece, compare its chosen height with the curve heights to its right.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"/alverstris/PROF-Skill.md-/blob/51a78beccef858072b1da8d057ef3dff09878409/runs/y1-reader-20261008/iterations/016/published-r26-20261010/fresh-r26b/teaching/lesson.md#p1\">Return to P1</a> · <a href=\"/alverstris/PROF-Skill.md-/blob/51a78beccef858072b1da8d057ef3dff09878409/runs/y1-reader-20261008/iterations/016/published-r26-20261010/fresh-r26b/teaching/solutions.md#s1\">Complete solution P1</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a id=\"user-content-h2\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hint P2. Write the right sum with square indices <math-renderer class=\"js-inline-math\" style=\"display: inline-block\" data-run-id=\"4e8f0daad35909a96fa97a069126732f\" data-catalyst=\"\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mo>…</mo>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mi>n</mi>\n</math></math-renderer> and the left sum with square indices <math-renderer class=\"js-inline-math\" style=\"display: inline-block\" data-run-id=\"4e8f0daad35909a96fa97a069126732f\" data-catalyst=\"\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>0</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mo>…</mo>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mi>n</mi>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mn>1</mn>\n</math></math-renderer>. Their common factor is <math-renderer class=\"js-inline-math\" style=\"display: inline-block\" data-run-id=\"4e8f0daad35909a96fa97a069126732f\" data-catalyst=\"\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msup>\n    <mi>b</mi>\n    <mn>3</mn>\n  </msup>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <msup>\n    <mi>n</mi>\n    <mn>3</mn>\n  </msup>\n</math></math-renderer>. Align the two lists before subtracting: only their unmatched endpoints remain. Then use that <math-renderer class=\"js-inline-math\" style=\"display: inline-block\" data-run-id=\"4e8f0daad35909a96fa97a069126732f\" data-catalyst=\"\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msup>\n    <mi>x</mi>\n    <mn>2</mn>\n  </msup>\n</math></math-renderer> is increasing on <math-renderer class=\"js-inline-math\" style=\"display: inline-block\" data-run-id=\"4e8f0daad35909a96fa97a069126732f\" data-catalyst=\"\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n  <mo>,</mo>\n  <mi>b</mi>\n  <mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo>\n</math></math-renderer> to place each sampled rectangle between its left and right counterparts.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"/alverstris/PROF-Skill.md-/blob/51a78beccef858072b1da8d057ef3dff09878409/runs/y1-reader-20261008/iterations/016/published-r26-20261010/fresh-r26b/teaching/lesson.md#p2\">Return to P2</a> · <a href=\"/alverstris/PROF-Skill.md-/blob/51a78beccef858072b1da8d057ef3dff09878409/runs/y1-reader-20261008/iterations/016/published-r26-20261010/fresh-r26b/teaching/solutions.md#s2\">Complete solution P2</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a id=\"user-content-h3\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hint P3. Match the sample coordinate <math-renderer class=\"js-inline-math\" style=\"display: inline-block\" data-run-id=\"4e8f0daad35909a96fa97a069126732f\" data-catalyst=\"\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo>+</mo>\n  <mn>3</mn>\n  <mi>i</mi>\n  <mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\">\n    <mo>/</mo>\n  </mrow>\n  <mi>n</mi>\n</math></math-renderer> to <math-renderer class=\"js-inline-math\" style=\"display: inline-block\" data-run-id=\"4e8f0daad35909a96fa97a069126732f\" data-catalyst=\"\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mi>a</mi>\n  <mo>+</mo>\n  <mi>i</mi>\n  <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi>\n  <mi>x</mi>\n</math></math-renderer>. Once you have the interval, solve <math-renderer class=\"js-inline-math\" style=\"display: inline-block\" data-run-id=\"4e8f0daad35909a96fa97a069126732f\" data-catalyst=\"\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>2</mn>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mi>x</mi>\n  <mo>=</mo>\n  <mn>0</mn>\n</math></math-renderer> to locate a possible sign change. The signed integral, the sum of positive geometric areas, and the signed integral divided by the interval length answer different questions.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"/alverstris/PROF-Skill.md-/blob/51a78beccef858072b1da8d057ef3dff09878409/runs/y1-reader-20261008/iterations/016/published-r26-20261010/fresh-r26b/teaching/lesson.md#p3\">Return to P3</a> · <a href=\"/alverstris/PROF-Skill.md-/blob/51a78beccef858072b1da8d057ef3dff09878409/runs/y1-reader-20261008/iterations/016/published-r26-20261010/fresh-r26b/teaching/solutions.md#s3\">Complete solution P3</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a id=\"user-content-h4\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hint P4. Start from the principal in one short interval, <math-renderer class=\"js-inline-math\" style=\"display: inline-block\" data-run-id=\"4e8f0daad35909a96fa97a069126732f\" data-catalyst=\"\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>12000</mn>\n  <mi>t</mi>\n  <mstyle>\n    <mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace>\n  </mstyle>\n  <mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi>\n  <mi>t</mi>\n</math></math-renderer> dollars. That portion has <math-renderer class=\"js-inline-math\" style=\"display: inline-block\" data-run-id=\"4e8f0daad35909a96fa97a069126732f\" data-catalyst=\"\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <mn>1</mn>\n  <mo>−</mo>\n  <mi>t</mi>\n</math></math-renderer> years to accrue simple interest. Multiply the portion by its own final-debt factor before adding. For the uniform comparison, replace the borrowing rate while keeping the same time-dependent factor.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"/alverstris/PROF-Skill.md-/blob/51a78beccef858072b1da8d057ef3dff09878409/runs/y1-reader-20261008/iterations/016/published-r26-20261010/fresh-r26b/teaching/lesson.md#p4\">Return to P4</a> · <a href=\"/alverstris/PROF-Skill.md-/blob/51a78beccef858072b1da8d057ef3dff09878409/runs/y1-reader-20261008/iterations/016/published-r26-20261010/fresh-r26b/teaching/solutions.md#s4\">Complete solution P4</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a id=\"user-content-h5\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hint P5. At a sample time <math-renderer class=\"js-inline-math\" style=\"display: inline-block\" data-run-id=\"4e8f0daad35909a96fa97a069126732f\" data-catalyst=\"\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\">\n  <msub>\n    <mi>c</mi>\n    <mi>i</mi>\n  </msub>\n</math></math-renderer>, the contribution is the signed rate there times the duration. Locate where the rate changes sign. For the amount moving either way, treat the magnitude of the outward contribution as positive; for net change retain its negative sign. The initial 10 litres and the four-minute duration enter different requested quantities.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"/alverstris/PROF-Skill.md-/blob/51a78beccef858072b1da8d057ef3dff09878409/runs/y1-reader-20261008/iterations/016/published-r26-20261010/fresh-r26b/teaching/lesson.md#p5\">Return to P5</a> · <a href=\"/alverstris/PROF-Skill.md-/blob/51a78beccef858072b1da8d057ef3dff09878409/runs/y1-reader-20261008/iterations/016/published-r26-20261010/fresh-r26b/teaching/solutions.md#s5\">Complete solution P5</a></p>\n</article>",
