      "text": "Hint P2. Write the right sum with square indices \n1\n,\n…\n,\n𝑛\n and the left sum with square indices \n0\n,\n…\n,\n𝑛\n−\n1\n. Their common factor is \n𝑏\n3\n/\n𝑛\n3\n. Align the two lists before subtracting: only their unmatched endpoints remain. Then use that \n𝑥\n2\n is increasing on \n[\n0\n,\n𝑏\n]\n to place each sampled rectangle between its left and right counterparts.",
