      "text": "Hint P5. At a sample time \n𝑐\n𝑖\n, the contribution is the signed rate there times the duration. Locate where the rate changes sign. For the amount moving either way, treat the magnitude of the outward contribution as positive; for net change retain its negative sign. The initial 10 litres and the four-minute duration enter different requested quantities.",
